	<string name="dlg_about_title">About Hot Death</string>
	<string name="dlg_about_text"><i>Version %s\nCopyright smorgasbork.com</i>\n\nHot Death is a variation of the classic card game, Uno.\n\nThis is a labor of love for me, as I have enjoyed the original Hot Death Uno for many years.  I first saw it in electronic form in the mid 90s, as a Visual Basic application for Windows.\n\nHere is the original "About" screen from that application (dated November 23, 1993):\n\n"Wow, you actually read "About" screens? I never do. Anyway, UNO is a trademark of Parker Brothers. Hot Death UNO was created by Byron Hoffman, John Howard, Chris Kulander, and Matt Murray; expanded by Keith Ammann, Larry Geraghty, Chris Kulander, Matt Murray, and Jason Seifert; and coded for Windows in Visual Basic by Mister Señor Love Daddy. I know this looks like shareware, but please do not send me any money or Parker Brothers might sue me. I didn't exactly get their permission to do this."\n\nInspired by the original, I wrote a version for Pocket PC in the early 2000s, and now it is here for Android.\n\nThis program is released as an open source project under the GPL (http://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl.html)\n\nTo access the source, visit http://www.smorgasbork.com/hotdeath/</string>
